CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ out-of-line member template body is used: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ member template body stored the value: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ member template body ran its statements: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^PARSING ERROR$
--
Out-of-line definition of a member function template of a class template
whose parameter names differ from the in-class declaration ([dcl.fct]/3).
The instantiated member must use the definition's parameter names for its
body; otherwise the body is ill-formed and silently dropped, leaving the
member with no body.
